Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:51:09 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 20/27] UPML operator: compute the coefficients on the setup
 threads (upstream PR #244)

Operator_Ext_UPML::BuildExtension() computed the PML coefficients of every cell on one thread, evaluating the
grading function through FunctionParser for every cell and component. The cells are independent:
BuildExtensionRange() now computes the x-lines of one thread, RunJobsInThreads() (tools/useful) splits the
x-lines over the operator's setup threads (GetNumSetupThreads(): the threads of the multithreaded operator, one
for the others), and each thread evaluates the grading on its own deep copy of the parser
(FunctionParser::Eval() is not reentrant). An exception in a thread is rethrown on the calling thread.

From upstream PR #244 by Noriaki Takashima (nori-proto): its UPML part and the RunJobsInThreads() helper, with
the thread count taken from GetNumSetupThreads() instead of AvailableThreads(), so the single-threaded engines
keep their one-thread setup. The PR's Debye part is not taken (no measurable share of any model's setup).

Same values in every cell (bit-identical). UPML build lap (OPENEMS_SETUP_TIMING=1, multithreaded engine, 6
interleaved rounds, other processes on 0.3-0.5 cores): SMA launch 0.086 -> 0.022 s (operator setup 0.32 ->
0.24 s), notch x3 0.090 -> 0.035 s (1.46 -> 1.38 s), notch tutorial 0.013 -> 0.005 s.

